{
  "about": "RLMesh v2 crypto interop vectors (design §8.8, DESIGN.md f3197f0). All byte strings are hex. Every fixed input (static and ephemeral private keys, the Ed25519 secret, Sealed keys, Ni, Nr) is BLAKE2s-256 of the UTF-8 string 'rlmesh/v2 vector: <name>' with the name given in `inputs`; pairing's 16-byte exchange id is the first 16 bytes of that hash for its name. Handshake ephemerals are what the injected RNG returned, so each side's draw is listed. Generated by crates/rlmesh-session-core/tests/crypto_vectors.rs (RLMESH_REGENERATE_CRYPTO_VECTORS=1), from rlmesh_session_core::crypto, except k_up/k_down and the XX split, which come from a separate snow replay with snow's own primitives; the same test cross-checks every vector with chacha20poly1305, ed25519-dalek, blake2 and snow directly. Sealed: nonce = kind || 3 zero bytes || seq u64 LE; AAD encrypted = header || lp(keyexpr), integrity-only = header || lp(keyexpr) || body with an empty plaintext. Signed: signature over lp(\"rlmesh/v2 signed\") || header || lp(keyexpr) || body; signed_view is a DeviceView (kind 22, scene design §3.4) whose body is the protobuf rlmesh.session.v2.DeviceView. IK: Noise_IK_25519_ChaChaPoly_BLAKE2s; k_up and k_down are the raw split (first = initiator to responder); sealed_up and sealed_down are one Sealed each way under them, sealed by the crate. Pairing: Noise_XX_25519_ChaChaPoly_BLAKE2s with prologue lp(\"rlmesh/v2 pair\") || exchange and empty payloads; key 1 = laptop to daemon (first split output).",
